>From all of the dozens of different authors, many of whom aren't
around anymore?

Good luck with that.

For myself, I don't much like share-alike licenses, and would
probably oppose any serious movement in that direction.

In practice, I treat the content as public domain.

We could put up a "by contributing, you agree to X" notice, the
problem is all the extant content.

-Robin

